# Unified grasp-planning request: any stable PrimitiveEstimate (CYLINDER,
# FLAT_BOX, or SPHERE - see GraspPlanner.PRIMITIVES) + its supporting point
# cloud, exactly as produced by /perception/get_stable_estimate.
pcl_package/PrimitiveEstimate estimate
sensor_msgs/PointCloud2 cloud
---
bool success
string reason

string primitive_type   # echoed back from the request, for convenience

geometry_msgs/Pose grasp_pose_palm
geometry_msgs/Pose grasp_pose_flange
geometry_msgs/Pose approach_pose_palm
geometry_msgs/Pose approach_pose_flange

# Confidence in the selected grasp, in [0.0, 1.0] (1.0 = best). Meaning
# depends on confidence_method:
#   "sector_residual" / "cap_residual" (CYLINDER / SPHERE): derived from how
#       well the visible point cloud fits the estimated radius right at the
#       predicted contact point. evidence_point_count is the number of cloud
#       points that supported the fit.
#   "width_centering" (FLAT_BOX): derived from how centered the grasp is on
#       the box's width, since a single-sided cloud gives no independent fit
#       metric to check against (see the node's module docstring).
#       evidence_point_count is always 0 for this method.
# Not directly comparable in an absolute sense across primitive types.
float64 confidence
string confidence_method
int32 evidence_point_count
bool met_confidence_threshold   # whether the primary point-count gate was met (always true for width_centering)
